    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d364">

                <pb facs="0298" n="286" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg286"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111A.R.–N.C./44: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hinkle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ciudad
                                Trujillo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-02-09T13:00:00-05:00">February 9, 1940—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>19. Department’s circular January 27, 3 p.m. Dominion [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dominican</hi>] Minister for Foreign Affairs<anchor n="43" xml:id="d364-f1"
                    /> today said that he would issue instructions shortly to his representative in
                    Rio which will be in accordance with the Department’s views on the Neutrality
                    Committee. The serious illness of the President during the past few weeks was,
                    according to the Secretary, delaying approval of such matters.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hinkle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
